Follow-up from the k190-192 review (M2, M3; ADR 0028).
1. Engine/Gemini.pm:406-415 still renames usageMetadata to snake_case in chat_response, although Usage->from_hash now reads promptTokenCount/candidatesTokenCount/totalTokenCount. ADR 0018 tier 1 says the universal door owns the spelling, so drop or simplify the engine rename.
2. Gemini emits cachedContentTokenCount as usage.cached_content_token_count, which from_hash never reads, so Gemini cached_tokens is always undef. Map cachedContentTokenCount (and/or cached_content_token_count) to cached_tokens.
3. Usage->from_raw recognizes Ollama top-level prompt_eval_count/eval_count but not AKI native top-level prompt_length/num_generated_tokens (Engine/AKI.pm:298). Decide whether they belong in from_raw (universal door) or stay engine-scoped. Nit: the Ollama probe uses defined, while Engine/Ollama.pm:288 uses truthiness, so prompt_eval_count 0 gives Usage(0) instead of undef.

Done on branch k197. Gemini rename kept: Usage %{} overload serves the engine hash verbatim, so usage->{prompt_tokens}/{cached_content_token_count} are public back-compat keys (CachedContent POD, t/47). from_hash maps both Gemini cache spellings; from_raw reads AKI native counts (incl. num_cached_tokens) and Ollama zero counts follow engine truthiness. No verbatim Gemini chat capture exists in t/data.

Fix round 1: Engine::AKI folds num_cached_tokens into its usage hash (Response->usage->cached_tokens == Response->cached_tokens == 16); from_hash reads flat cached_tokens last; from_raw keeps cache-only AKI bodies; legacy-keys POD note; ADR 0028 update corrected.

